{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "John startled awake, his vision blurring before snapping into sharp, pixelated clarity. The world around him was a vibrant, albeit low-resolution, landscape of rolling green hills and a clear blue sky, the sun casting long shadows in a manner that felt both familiar and alien. He looked down at his hands, which now appeared as blocky, colored polygons rather than the flesh and bone he remembered. Panic surged as he realized he couldn’t feel the ground beneath his feet, nor could he hear anything beyond the faint, synthesized hum of an old video game soundtrack. His heart raced—not in his chest, but somewhere deep in the mechanical depths of this digital prison.\n\n***\n\nDesperate for answers, John stumbled toward the nearest village, his movements stiff and unnatural, as if he were a puppet on invisible strings. The villagers, with their oversized heads and tiny bodies, went about their day oblivious to his plight, chatting in a language that sounded like a mix of beeps and chatter. He tried to speak, but his words came out as garbled text on the screen, eliciting confused glances from the NPCs. A child pointed at him and giggled before running off, leaving John alone with the crushing realization that no one here could help him—or even comprehend his existence. The weight of his digital imprisonment settled over him like a suffocating blanket, and he wondered if he’d ever wake up again, or if this was his new reality.", "logprobs": [{"token": "John", "logprob": -1.5761476755142212}, {"token": " startled", "logprob": -3.162060499191284}, {"token": " awake", "logprob": -0.0010288427583873272}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.21010497212409973}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.10627070814371109}, {"token": " vision", "logprob": -0.8988575339317322}, {"token": " bl", "logprob": -1.553156852722168}, {"token": "urring", "logprob": -0.575969159603118